.TH NVIMI 1 "November 2026" "nvimi 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.nh
.SH NAME
nvimi \- rank and reopen files from the nvimpp launch history
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nvimi
.RB [ \-h | \-v | \-c ]
.RB [ stats | history ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nvimi
reads the history written by
.BR nvimpp (1).
Without a mode it shows an inline picker below the prompt, with files ranked by frecency (frequency weighted by recency).
Each row shows how many times the file was opened, its score and its path.
Rows marked
.B dashboard
are launches without a file; selecting one opens Neovim in that folder.
.PP
The selected entry is opened through
.BR nvimpp (1),
so the pick is recorded as a new launch.
.SH MODES
.TP
.I (none)
Inline picker ranked by frecency.
In this mode the history file is also trimmed when it has grown past its limit.
.TP
.B stats
Print every file ranked by the number of launches, followed by the total number of launches and of distinct files.
.TP
.B history
Print every launch with its date, the time elapsed since then, and the arguments as typed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a short help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config
Print the configuration file and exit.
.SH PICKER KEYS
.TP
.BR j ", Down"
Move down.
.TP
.BR k ", Up"
Move up.
.TP
.B Enter
Open the selected entry.
.TP
.BR q ", Esc, Ctrl-C"
Quit without opening anything.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.B nvimi
reads the same configuration file as
.BR nvimpp (1).
If the file is missing, a warning is printed and the defaults are used; a key missing from the file also keeps its default.
.TP
.B limit
Number of history lines kept after a trim.
.TP
.B wait
Number of lines allowed past
.I limit
before the next trim.
.TP
.B rows
Maximum number of rows in the picker.
.TP
.B halflife_days
Half-life of the frecency score, in days.
.SH SCORING
Each recorded launch adds 0.5^(age/half-life) to the score of its file, where age is the time elapsed since that launch.
With a half-life of 7 days, a launch from today counts 1 and one from a week ago counts 0.5.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/nvimpp/nvimpp.config
Configuration file.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/nvimpp/history_nvim.csv
History file written by
.BR nvimpp (1).
Malformed lines are skipped.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B HOME
Used to locate the configuration and history files.
.B nvimi
exits with an error if it is not set.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, or the picker was closed without a selection.
.TP
.B 1
Invalid argument or option,
.B HOME
not set, history file missing, or
.B \-c
with no configuration file.
.TP
.B 2
Internal error: no mode selected.
.TP
.B 4
No terminal available for the picker
.RI ( /dev/tty ).
.TP
.B 5
Changing to the folder of a dashboard entry failed.
.TP
.B 127
.BR nvimpp (1)
could not be started.
.PP
When an entry is opened,
.B nvimi
is replaced by
.BR nvimpp (1),
so the exit status is that of Neovim.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B nvimi
Pick a recent file and open it.
.TP
.B nvimi stats
See which files are opened most.
.TP
.B nvimi history | less \-R
Browse the full launch history with colors.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nvimpp (1),
.BR nvim (1)
